@startuml
title Digital Credential Issuance part 1 : request until offer link (SD-JWT VC, HSM-backed Issuer, On-Device Credential Model)
bottomparticipants

participant User
participant "Mobile App (Core ทางรัฐ)" as CoreApp #lightblue
participant "Document Wallet (Miniapp)" as Mini #lightblue
participant "DW Core" as DW #lightcyan
participant "Government API Source of Truth" as Agency #lightgray
participant "VCVP Core" as Core #lightgreen
participant "one-core (Credential Engine)" as Engine #orange
participant "HSM" as HSM #yellow
participant "Trust Registry ETDA" as Trust #violet

note over Engine,HSM #wheat:[SPEC] Issuer signing keys are HSM-backed\nPrivate key is generated inside HSM\nPrivate key never leaves HSM\nEngine stores key metadata and HSM reference\nVCVP Core receives ISSUER_KEY_ID and publicKey only\n[IN DEVELOPMENT] engine v1.86.1 key storage supports only INTERNAL , AZURE_VAULT , SIGN8\nSECURE_ELEMENT , REMOTE_SECURE_ELEMENT , no HSM , PKCS11 removed since v1.78.2

note over User,CoreApp #lightblue: 1.1 User Login
User->CoreApp: Login (PIN / biometric)
CoreApp->CoreApp: Login with Tang Rat to get Token
CoreApp-->User: Login completed , show Tang Rat home

note over CoreApp,DW #lightblue: 1.2 Request VC Issuance
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] A card/document is added to the wallet only when both conditions hold\n1. applicant data is linked from the government source of truth (section 2)\n2. the VC is issued and verified by the wallet (sections 8 , 9)\nAny problem in VC issuance returns an error to the wallet , the wallet stops\nNo card/document is added without a VC
User->Mini: Choose a card/document to add
Mini->CoreApp: Check holder key exists on this device
CoreApp->CoreApp: Check holder key exists on this device\n(key alias in Android Keystore / Secure Enclave)
CoreApp-->Mini: Holder key found / not found
alt Holder key not found on device (first use of Document Wallet on this device)
    Mini->CoreApp: Create and register the holder key
    CoreApp->DW: Request holder key registration challenge + Token | POST /dw/v1/holder-keys/challenge (DW endpoint 01)\n(deviceId)
    DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store challenge in DW database
    CoreApp<--DW: challengeId , nonce , expiresAt
    CoreApp->CoreApp: Generate holder key pair (Secure Enclave / Android Keystore / StrongBox)\nSign challenge with holder private key
    CoreApp->DW: Submit holder proof + Token | POST /dw/v1/holder-keys/register (DW endpoint 02)\n(signedChallenge , challengeId , publicKey)
    DW->DW: Verify signed challenge with publicKey\n[DATA STORE] Store holder public key , device status = HOLDER_BOUND
    CoreApp<--DW: Holder key registered
    note right of CoreApp #wheat:[SPEC] OpenID4VCI 1.0 Appendix D key attestation : a statement signed by the wallet provider that the holder key is kept in secure hardware\nRequired when the schema sets KeyStorageSecurity , the level in the attestation must match it\nThe wallet provider here is the wallet provider of the engine , run by VCVP
    CoreApp->Core: Register wallet unit | POST /ssi/wallet-unit/v1\n(walletProvider , os) , no public key or proof because the app integrity check is on
    Core->Engine: Register wallet unit | POST /ssi/wallet-unit/v1
    Engine-->Core: wallet unit id , nonce
    CoreApp<--Core: wallet unit id , nonce
    CoreApp->CoreApp: Create the attestation key with the nonce as challenge and get the platform attestation\nAndroid Key Attestation (StrongBox) / iOS App Attest
    CoreApp->Core: Activate wallet unit | POST /ssi/wallet-unit/v1/{id}/activate\n(attestation , attestation key proof , device signing key proof)
    Core->Engine: Activate wallet unit | POST /ssi/wallet-unit/v1/{id}/activate
    Engine->Engine: Check app integrity\nAndroid : Google attestation CA , bundleId , signing certificate fingerprint , StrongBox\niOS : Apple App Attest root CA , bundleId
    note right of Engine #wheat:[ENGINE RULE] Android keys kept only in TEE (no StrongBox) are refused (insufficient security level)
    note right of Engine #wheat:[PENDING] For team discussion : Android devices without StrongBox cannot activate the wallet
    alt App integrity check failed (e.g. Android without StrongBox)
        Engine->Engine: Set wallet unit status = ERROR
        Engine-->Core: Error
        CoreApp<--Core: Error
        CoreApp-->Mini: Wallet cannot be activated on this device
        Mini-->User: Show error , card/document with a VC cannot be added on this device
        note over User,Mini #wheat: Issuance stops here , sections 1.3 to 11 do not apply
    else App integrity check passed
        Engine-->Core: Wallet unit activated
        CoreApp<--Core: Wallet unit activated
    end
    CoreApp->Core: Request key attestation | POST /ssi/wallet-unit/v1/{id}/issue-attestation\n(wua : proof signed with the holder key , security_level)
    Core->Engine: Request key attestation | POST /ssi/wallet-unit/v1/{id}/issue-attestation
    Engine->Engine: Sign key attestation (WUA) with the wallet provider key\nattested_keys = holder public key , key_storage = requested level\nvalid 31 days , revocable (Token Status List)
    Engine-->Core: WUA (key-attestation+jwt)
    CoreApp<--Core: WUA
    CoreApp->CoreApp: [DATA STORE] Store WUA with the holder key
    note right of CoreApp #wheat:[PENDING] security_level the app requests : the level set on the schemas (one level in phase 1)
    CoreApp-->Mini: Holder key registered
else Holder key found
    Mini->Mini: Continue
end
note right of Mini #wheat:[SPEC] Key found on the device does not confirm it is registered in DW\nDW checks registration by deviceId below
note right of Mini #wheat:[PENDING] For team discussion : the wallet does not send identity assurance to DW today\nHow the wallet logs in and obtains the IdP ID token is part of the wallet, the wallet\nteam must decide where the code is exchanged
Mini->DW:Request to add card / document + Token (from Tang Rat login) | POST /v1/virtualcards/sync_queue_list (DW endpoint 03) (deviceId registered with the holder key)\n[PENDING] + IdP ID token
Mini-->User: Show processing (wait for response of 1.2)
DW->DW: Validate Token to get CitizenId
note right of DW #wheat:[DATA STORE] DW database (issuance request)\nissuanceSessionId (created by DW)\nCitizenId (from Token)\ndeviceId\nrequested card / document\nstatus\nrequestedAt
DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store issuance request in DW database
DW->DW: Look up holder key of this device in DW database\n(look up by deviceId , device status = HOLDER_BOUND)

alt Holder key of this device not registered
    note right of DW #wheat:Response of 1.2 tells the app to register the holder key again (same steps as 1.2)\nso the next request can receive the card/document with a VC
    DW->DW: Mark VC not possible (reason = WALLET_NOT_ACTIVATED)\nno response yet , the error is returned in section 2.1
else Holder key registered
    DW->DW: Continue to 1.3
end

note over DW #lightblue: 1.3 Validate Existing Identity Assurance

alt IdP ID token provided (PENDING)
    DW->DW: [PENDING] Load IdP signing keys (IdP jwks_uri , cached)
    DW->DW: Verify ID token\nsignature (IdP JWKS , ES256) , iss = IdP , aud = client_id registered with the IdP , exp , nonce
    DW->DW: Check pid in ID token = CitizenId from Token

    alt ID token invalid / pid mismatch
        DW->DW: Update issuance request status = IDENTITY_ASSURANCE_INVALID
        DW->DW: [ERROR AUDIT] Store DW audit log (FailureReason = IDENTITY_ASSURANCE_INVALID)
        Mini<--DW: Reject issuance request\nreason = IDENTITY_ASSURANCE_INVALID
        Mini-->User: Cannot proceed , please log in again
    else ID token valid
        note right of DW #wheat:[DATA STORE] DW database (identity assurance profile)\nial stored as IAL level\niss stored as KYC source\nauth_time stored as last authentication timestamp\namr stored as last authentication method (if provided)\npid stored as citizenId\nissued ID token reference (jti) stored in audit
        DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store identity assurance profile in DW database
    end
else No IdP ID token (existing session)
    DW->DW: Use identity assurance profile stored at last login
end

note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] Identity assurance profile in DW database\nidentityAssuranceId\ncitizenId\nIAL level\nAAL level\nKYC source\nKYC timestamp\nassurance expiry\nlast authentication method\nlast authentication timestamp
DW->DW: Load existing identity assurance profile

DW->DW: Check VC possible for this request (mark set in 1.2)
alt VC already marked not possible in 1.2 (WALLET_NOT_ACTIVATED)
    DW->DW: Skip RequiredLoA check and step-up\n(the request already failed in 1.2 , it ends with an error in section 2.1)
else VC still possible
    note right of DW #wheat:[PENDING] RequiredLoA is set by the issuing agency on the schema\nNot taken from the Trust Registry , its LoA support is not known yet
    DW->DW: [PENDING] Get RequiredLoA of the requested document from DW catalog\n(DocumentSchemas.RequiredLoA via document-schemas/list)
    DW->DW: Validate assurance\nstill valid (assurance expiry) , meets required freshness ,\nIAL level ≥ RequiredLoA

    alt Assurance invalid / expired / not fresh / IAL below RequiredLoA
        DW->DW: Update issuance request status = STEP_UP_REQUIRED\n(VC not issued , this request ends here)
        Mini<--DW: Response of 1.2 : request step-up verification or re-KYC | reason , RequiredLoA
        Mini-->User: Show message : identity verification is not enough for this card/document (reason , RequiredLoA)\nask the user to verify identity again in Tang Rat before continuing
        Mini->DW: Submit verification result (new IdP ID token) | POST /dw/v1/identity-assurance/step-up (DW endpoint 04)
        DW->DW: Verify new ID token (same checks as above)
        DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store updated identity assurance profile in DW database
        DW->DW: Validate assurance again

        alt Still not sufficient
            DW->DW: [ERROR AUDIT] Store DW audit log (FailureReason = LOA_INSUFFICIENT)
            Mini<--DW: Error (response of step-up) | reason = LOA_INSUFFICIENT
            Mini-->User: Show error , card/document not added (reason)
        else Assurance sufficient
            Mini<--DW: 200 (response of step-up)
            Mini->Mini: Send request 1.2 again for the same card/document\n(the new request runs from section 1.2 with the updated identity assurance)
        end
        note over User,Mini #wheat: This request stops here , sections 2 to 11 do not apply to it

    else Assurance valid
        DW->DW: Continue to Read Data
    end
end

note over DW,Agency #lightgray: 2. Read Official card / document
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] Use user session\nuserId\ncitizenId\naccess token
DW->DW: Look up applicant data in DW database

alt No data in DW database
    note right of Agency #wheat:[SPEC] Retrieve official card/document data\nfrom government source of truth
    DW->Agency:Fetch applicant data from agency

    alt Data not found / not authorized
        DW<--Agency: Not found | Not authorized
        DW->DW: [ERROR AUDIT] Store DW audit log (FailureReason = AGENCY_DATA_NOT_FOUND / AGENCY_NOT_AUTHORIZED)
        Mini<--DW: Return reason (Not found 404 | Not authorized 403)
        Mini-->User: Show reason (Not found 404 | Not authorized 403)
    else Agency data available
        DW<--Agency: Applicant data + SyncDate
        note right of DW #wheat:[DATA STORE] DW database\nsourceFetchedAt = SyncDate\nsourceLastUpdatedAt = from agency if available\nsourceSystem = Government API Source of Truth\ncachePolicy = reuse data in DW database if it already exists\ncacheKey = citizenId + documentType\ncacheInvalidation = on revoke / suspend / expire
        DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store applicant data + SyncDate in DW database
    end

else Data already exists
    DW->DW: Use applicant data from DW database
end

DW->DW: Validate official data & Check status active & Check not suspended &\nCheck not revoked etc.

alt Official card/document invalid
    DW->DW: Update status SOURCE_DATA_INVALID
    DW->DW: [ERROR AUDIT] Store DW audit log (FailureReason = SOURCE_DATA_INVALID)
    Mini<--DW: Reject issuance request
    Mini-->User: card/document not eligible
else Official card/document valid
    DW->DW: Prepare verified claims
end

note over CoreApp,DW #lightgray: 2.1 Check VC is possible before issuing
DW->DW: Check VC possible for this request (mark set in 1.2)
alt VC not possible (WALLET_NOT_ACTIVATED from 1.2)
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = WALLET_NOT_ACTIVATED\n(VC not issued , card/document not added)
    DW->DW: [ERROR AUDIT] Store DW audit log (FailureReason = WALLET_NOT_ACTIVATED)
    Mini<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = WALLET_NOT_ACTIVATED\nnextAction = REGISTER_HOLDER_KEY
    Mini-->User: Show error , card/document not added (reason)
    Mini->CoreApp: Register the holder key again (same steps as 1.2)\nso the user can request the card/document again
    CoreApp-->Mini: Holder key registered
    note over User,Mini #wheat: Issuance stops here , card/document not added , sections 3 to 11 do not apply
else VC possible
    DW->DW: Continue to section 3 (get schema details)
end

note over DW,Engine #violet: 3. Get Schema Details
note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Get schema details and request issuance are used by two callers :\nDW Core (this flow) and agency systems that call VCVP Core directly (system to system issuance)\nSteps marked "caller channel = WALLET" run only for requests from DW Core\nDW Core returns the error to the app , VCVP Core only returns the reason
note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] VCVP Core writes an access log for every request\nincluding requests rejected at the Consumer-Key check (e.g. invalid Consumer-Key) , these get no audit record\nVCVPAuditLog holds only requests that pass the Consumer-Key check
DW->Core: Get schema details | POST /vcvp/v1/document-schemas/get (VCVP Core 07)
Core->Core: Check Consumer-Key (DW Core central Consumer-Key) , caller channel = WALLET , ActorType = CITIZEN\nwrite access log
Core->Core: Validate the Consumer-Key may call this endpoint
alt Caller not authorized
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 07 (FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED)
    DW<--Core: 403 | FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED\n(VC not issued , card/document not added)
    Mini<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
    Mini-->User: Show error , card/document not added (reason)
    note over User,Mini #wheat: Issuance stops here , card/document not added , sections 3 to 11 do not apply
else Caller authorized
    Core->Core: Continue to Read Schema
end
note over DW,Engine #orange: 3.1 Read Schema
Core->Core: Look up card/document schema in DocumentSchemas table
alt Schema not found
    note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] The credential schema must be created by the issuing agency\nVCVP does not create a schema during issuance
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 07 (FailureReason = SCHEMA_NOT_FOUND , EngineCalls)
    DW<--Core: 404 | FailureReason = SCHEMA_NOT_FOUND
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = SCHEMA_NOT_FOUND\n(VC not issued , card/document not added)
    Mini<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = SCHEMA_NOT_FOUND
    Mini-->User: Show error , card/document not added (reason)
    note over User,Mini #wheat: Issuance stops here , card/document not added , sections 3.2 to 11 do not apply
else Schema found
    Core->Core: Map DocumentSchemaId to engine CREDENTIAL_SCHEMA_ID and the engine to call\n(DocumentSchemas.EngineRefs[].RefDocumentSchemaId , EngineRefs[].EngineName)
    note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] DW Core requests system to system with one central Consumer-Key for all agencies\nThe WALLET Consumer-Key is issued only by VCVP administrators , only to DW Core\nThe agency opts in per schema when creating it\nChecked again when issuance is requested (section 5)
    Core->Core: Check permission by caller channel\nWALLET (DW central Consumer-Key) : the agency allows requests from the wallet on this schema (DocumentSchemas.AllowWalletRequest)\nother channels : the schema belongs to the caller's organisation

    alt Wallet request not allowed by the agency
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 07 (FailureReason = WALLET_REQUEST_NOT_ALLOWED , EngineCalls)
        DW<--Core: 403 | FailureReason = WALLET_REQUEST_NOT_ALLOWED
        DW->DW: Update issuance request status = WALLET_REQUEST_NOT_ALLOWED\n(VC not issued , card/document not added)
        Mini<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = WALLET_REQUEST_NOT_ALLOWED
        Mini-->User: Show error , card/document not added (reason)
        note over User,Mini #wheat: Issuance stops here , card/document not added , sections 3.2 to 11 do not apply
    else Wallet request allowed
        Core->Core: Continue to read schema details
    end
end


note over DW,Engine #orange: 3.2 Read Schema Details
note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Defined on the schema , not on the issuance request (engine name stored in DocumentSchemas field)\nformats[] sets the format to SD_JWT_VC (stored in Formats[].Format)\nallowSuspension must be set to true explicitly , otherwise the credential cannot be suspended (stored in Suspendable)\nRevocation method is not stored in the schema , it comes from config that binds SD_JWT_VC to TOKENSTATUSLIST (stored in Formats[].RevocationMethod)\nEach claim has a technicalKey separate from key , e.g. LicenseNumber -> license_number (stored in Claims[].Path , Claims[].Mappings[].TechnicalKey)\nThe name that appears in the credential is the technicalKey
Core->Engine: Get schema details | GET /api/credential-schema/v2/{id} (VCVP Core 07) ({id} = CREDENTIAL_SCHEMA_ID from DocumentSchemas.EngineRefs[].RefDocumentSchemaId)
Core<--Engine: 200 | schema details + Claims[] (ClaimId | Path | Name | Type | Required)
Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of VCVP Core 07 (EngineCalls)
DW<--Core: 200 | schema details + Claims[] (ClaimId | Path | NameEn | NameLocal | Type | Required)

note over DW #lightgreen: 4. Prepare Data
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] Map fields to claim IDs
DW->DW: Map data to Claims[] based on schema details from VCVP Core 07\nSet OrgCode of the issuing agency\n(IssuerIdentityId and IssuerKey are not sent , VCVP Core selects them in section 5.1)

note right of DW #wheat:[AUDIT LOG] auditHash = hash(canonical audit payload)\nauditSignature = sign(auditHash) (optional)\npreviousAuditHash = link to previous log\nretentionPolicy = e.g. 10 years or regulatory requirement\nretentionUntil = issuedAt + retention period\nimmutableStorage = WORM / append-only log
DW->DW: Create tamper-evident audit record of the mapped claims (DW audit log)
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] ISO/IEC 27002:2022 8.15 Logging (ISO/IEC 27001:2022 Annex A 8.15)\nlogs of activities , exceptions , faults and other relevant events are produced , stored , protected and analysed\nlog protection : cryptographic hashing , append-only recording , read-only recording , public transparency files\nusers cannot delete or amend logs of their own activities\nISO/IEC 27701:2025 A.3.25 Logging (guidance B.3.25)\nlogs of PII processing record who accessed PII , when , whose PII and what was added , changed or deleted\nlogs can contain PII : access is controlled , used only as intended , deleted or de-identified by the retention schedule\nThai MDES notice on keeping computer traffic data B.E. 2564 clause 9 : storage keeps integrity and identifies who accessed it\nadministrators cannot modify stored data (e.g. centralized log server , data archiving , data hashing) | clause 12 : keep at least 90 days\nNo checked source requires signing the hash , so auditSignature is optional\nSource limitation : ISO wording taken from secondary summaries (isms.online , checked 11 Oct 2026) , not from the ISO text itself\nISO standards are sold per copy , confirm the wording against the purchased ISO/IEC 27002:2022 and ISO/IEC 27701:2025 before citing in an audit

note right of DW #wheat:[DATA STORE] DW database\nissuance request\nmapped claims\naudit log\nidentity assurance reference
DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store mapped claims + audit log in DW database (issuance request)

note over DW,Core #lightgreen: 5. Request Issuance and Validate Request
DW->Core: Request credential issuance | POST /vcvp/v1/documents (VCVP Core 08)
Core->Core: Check Consumer-Key (DW Core central Consumer-Key) , caller channel = WALLET , ActorType = CITIZEN\nwrite access log
Core->Core: Validate caller authorization\nallowed to issue this VC type on behalf of this organisation\n(caller channel WALLET : DocumentSchemas.AllowWalletRequest = true)
Core->Core: Validate tenant scope\nreferenced data belongs to the caller's organisation
note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Claim name restrictions are enforced at schema creation , not at issuance\nName must not be "0" | must not contain / because it separates nested claim levels\nTotal key length must not exceed 255 characters
note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Engine key has no status or expiresAt (only id , createdDate , lastModified , organisationId\nname , publicKey , keyType , storageType , isRemote , autogenerated)\nKey status is kept in the VCVP Keys table : RESERVED / ACTIVE / DEPRECATED / REVOKED
Core->Core: Validate claims against schema | Validate key matches identity (Keys.IdentityId , if IssuerKey sent)\nCitizenId to CitizenHashId

alt Request invalid / unauthorized
    note right of Core #wheat:[ERROR AUDIT] VCVPAuditLog\nFailureReason = REQUEST_REJECTED\nMessageCode , Message (HTTP status of the error)\nEventTime\nActor (OrgCode , ConsumerKey , Channel)\nCorrelation.RequestId
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 08 (FailureReason = REQUEST_REJECTED)

    DW<--Core: Reject issuance request
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = REQUEST_REJECTED\n(VC not issued , card/document not added)
    Mini<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = REQUEST_REJECTED
    Mini-->User: Show error , card/document not added (reason)
else Request valid
    Core->Core: Continue issuance
end

note over Core,HSM #orange: 5.1 Check Issuer Setup

note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Organisation , issuer key and DID must be prepared by the issuing agency in the setup phase\nVCVP does not create them during issuance\nIf any of them is missing , VC is not issued and the card/document is not added

Core->Core: Look up agency organisation in Organizations table (OrgCode)
Core->Core: Select issuer DID from the schema\n(DocumentSchemas.IssuerIdentityId)\nuse IssuerIdentityId instead if the caller sent it\nengine to call = DocumentSchemas.EngineRefs[].EngineName
note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Issuer key status : RESERVED / ACTIVE / DEPRECATED / REVOKED\nRESERVED = key placed in the DID at creation , not used for signing yet\nOnly one ACTIVE key per identity (unique index on IdentityId + Status = ACTIVE)\nNo ACTIVE key → handled in section 5.2 (switch to the next RESERVED key)\nMore than one ACTIVE key → configuration error , do not guess\nVCVP Core always sends issuer and issuerKey to the engine , never relies on the engine default (first key in the DID)
Core->Core: Select issuer key = the ACTIVE key of that DID\n(Keys.Status = ACTIVE , Keys.IdentityId)\nuse IssuerKey instead if the caller sent it

alt Organisation / issuer DID not found , or more than one ACTIVE key
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 08\n(FailureReason = ORGANISATION_NOT_FOUND / ISSUER_DID_NOT_FOUND / ISSUER_KEY_AMBIGUOUS)
    DW<--Core: Reject issuance request\nFailureReason = ORGANISATION_NOT_FOUND / ISSUER_DID_NOT_FOUND / ISSUER_KEY_AMBIGUOUS
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = ISSUER_SETUP_NOT_FOUND\n(VC not issued , card/document not added)
    Mini<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = ISSUER_SETUP_NOT_FOUND
    Mini-->User: Show error , card/document not added (reason)
    note over User,Mini #wheat: Issuance stops here , card/document not added , sections 5.1.1 to 11 do not apply
else Organisation and issuer DID found , at most one ACTIVE key
    Core->Core: Use ORG_ID , ISSUER_IDENTIFIER_ID , ISSUER_KEY_ID (ACTIVE key , if any)
end

note over Core,Trust #violet: 5.1.1 Check Trust Framework
note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Thai VC ARF v1.1 section 3.3 and ETDA digital wallet draft v0.2 section 3.3 : the holder and the verifier look up the issuer in the registry\nThis check at issuance is a VCVP policy , the wallet still checks the issuer in section 9
Core->Trust: Check issuer DID is listed and accreditation not expired | GET {trust registry URL}\n(issuer DID selected in section 5.1)
Trust-->Core: Accreditation status
note right of Core #wheat:[AUDIT LOG] VCVPAuditLog (TrustCheck)\ntrust validation result stored in TrustCheck.Result\ntimestamp stored in TrustCheck.CheckedAt\ntrust registry reference stored in TrustCheck.RegistryReference\nWritten once with the audit record of this request , never updated
Core->Core: Keep trust validation result (for the audit record of VCVP Core 08)
Core->Core: Validate issuer is listed and accreditation not expired
alt Trust validation failed
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 08 (FailureReason = TRUST_FAILED , TrustCheck)
    DW<--Core: 403 | FailureReason = TRUST_FAILED
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = TRUST_FAILED\n(VC not issued , card/document not added)
    Mini<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = TRUST_FAILED
    Mini-->User: Show error , card/document not added (reason)
    note over User,Mini #wheat: Issuance stops here , card/document not added , sections 5.2 to 11 do not apply
else Trust validation passed
    Core->Core: Continue issuance
end


note over Core,HSM #orange: 5.2 Credential Lifecycle Policy and Issuer Key Check

note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Validity is defined on the schema (expiration) , not per credential\nRevocation method comes from config bound to the format (SD_JWT_VC to TOKENSTATUSLIST)
Core->Core: Read credential metadata & validFrom & validUntil &\nrevocation status method & credential lifecycle policy from schema / config\nand record in Documents table

Core->Core: Get issuer key metadata from VCVP Keys table\nkey status , createdAt , expiresAt

note right of Engine #wheat:[SPEC] DID can have multiple keys (verification methods)\nAll keys must be included when the DID is created (up to 5)\nEngine has no identifier update API (only POST , GET , DELETE , list , /remote , resolve-trust-entries)\nKeys cannot be added to an existing DID\nKeys can be rotated without changing DID by switching issuerKey to a key already in the DID
alt No ACTIVE key / key expired / near expiry / inactive

    alt Next key reserved in the issuer DID is available
        Core->Core: Switch issuerKey to the next reserved key in the DID\n(Keys.Status RESERVED → ACTIVE)
    else No reserved key left in the DID
        note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] VCVP does not create a new key or DID during issuance\nThe existing DID cannot be updated , so new keys need a new DID\nThe issuing agency creates the new key and DID in the setup phase\nand registers the new DID in the Trust Registry before use
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 08 (FailureReason = ISSUER_KEY_EXPIRED)

        DW<--Core: Reject issuance request\nFailureReason = ISSUER_KEY_EXPIRED
        DW->DW: Update issuance request status = ISSUER_KEY_EXPIRED\n(VC not issued , card/document not added)
        Mini<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = ISSUER_KEY_EXPIRED
        Mini-->User: Show error , card/document not added (reason)
        note over User,Mini #wheat: Issuance stops here , card/document not added , sections 6 to 11 do not apply
    end

    note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Keep old ISSUER_KEY_ID available for verifying previously issued credentials\nOld key status = DEPRECATED, not revoked\nUse new ISSUER_KEY_ID for new credential issuance only\nRevoke old key only if compromised
    Core->Core: Mark old ISSUER_KEY_ID as DEPRECATED

else Key active
    Core->Core: Continue issuance
end

note over Core,Engine #orange: 6. Create Digital Credential and Offer
Core->Core: Use ClaimId from the request as the engine claim id\n(DocumentSchemas.Claims[].ClaimId is the claim id created by the engine)
note right of Engine #wheat:[IMPORTANT] Nothing is signed at this step , no status list index is reserved and no token exists yet\nState is CREATED and the credential field is empty\nThis request has no format , proofType , cnf or revocation method parameter\nformat and revocation method come from schema and config | cnf comes from the wallet proof at credential request\nissuer takes the engine IdentifierId , not the did:web value\nCredential expiry cannot be set per credential
Core->Engine: Create credential | POST /api/credential/v1 (VCVP Core 08)\ncredentialSchemaId , issuer = agency IdentifierId (did:web) , issuerKey\nprotocol = OPENID4VCI_FINAL1\nclaimValues [ claimId , path , value ]
Engine-->Core: { id } = CREDENTIAL_ID

note right of Core #wheat:[DATA STORE] Documents table\nCREDENTIAL_ID stored in EngineRefs[].RefDocumentId (+ EngineRefs[].EngineName)\nDocumentSchemaId , IssuerOrganizationId , IssuerIdentityId , CitizenHashId , SyncDate
Core->Core: [DATA STORE] Store document in Documents table
note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] credential_offer_uri points to\n/ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/offer/{credentialId}\nThe offer contains credential_issuer , credential_configuration_ids (the vct URL)\nand grants.pre-authorized_code\ntransaction_code is not used , so the offer has no such field\nEngine state changes from CREATED to PENDING after this call
Core->Engine: Create offer link | POST /api/credential/v1/{CREDENTIAL_ID}/share (VCVP Core 08) (CREDENTIAL_ID from Documents table EngineRefs[].RefDocumentId)
alt Offer link not created (engine error)
    Engine-->Core: Error
    Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of VCVP Core 08 (TrustCheck , EngineCalls , Correlation.DocumentId)
    DW<--Core: 200 | DocumentId , OfferUrl = null , IssuerTrust (Result , CheckedAt , RegistryReference)
    DW->Core: Request offer link | POST /vcvp/v1/documents/offer (VCVP Core 09) (DocumentId)
    Core->Core: Check Consumer-Key (DW Core central Consumer-Key) , caller channel = WALLET , ActorType = CITIZEN\nwrite access log\nValidate caller authorization
    Core->Engine: Create offer link | POST /api/credential/v1/{CREDENTIAL_ID}/share (VCVP Core 09)
    Engine-->Core: url , expiresAt
    Core->Core: [DATA STORE] Store offer in Documents table\n[AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of VCVP Core 09 (EngineCalls , Correlation.DocumentId)
    DW<--Core: 200 | DocumentId + OfferUrl + ExpiresAt
else Offer link created
    Engine-->Core: url = openid-credential-offer://?credential_offer_uri=...\nexpiresAt
    note right of Core #wheat:[DATA STORE] Documents table\nCREDENTIAL_ID stored in EngineRefs[].RefDocumentId\nurl stored in OfferUrl (temporary)\nexpiresAt stored in OfferExpiresAt\nStatus = PENDING
    Core->Core: [DATA STORE] Store offer in Documents table
    Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of VCVP Core 08 (TrustCheck , EngineCalls , Correlation.DocumentId)
    DW<--Core: 200 | DocumentId + OfferUrl + ExpiresAt + IssuerTrust (Result , CheckedAt , RegistryReference)
end
note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Offer expiry\nThe engine does not tell VCVP when an offer expires (credential webhook is sent only for ACCEPTED , SUSPENDED , REVOKED , REJECTED , ERROR)\nThe engine sets INTERACTION_EXPIRED only when its task INTERACTION_EXPIRATION_CHECK is run (POST /api/task/v1/run , scheduled by ops)\nVCVP Core scheduled job : Documents with Status = PENDING and OfferExpiresAt passed , read the engine state first\nengine PENDING or INTERACTION_EXPIRED : Status PENDING → OFFER_EXPIRED | engine OFFERED : keep Status = PENDING\nA renewed offer link sets Status back to PENDING | credential_accepted later still sets Status to ACTIVE\nA credential already in OFFERED (token exchanged) stays OFFERED , the holder can still get the credential with its access token
DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store DocumentId + OfferUrl + ExpiresAt + IssuerTrust in DW database (issuance request)\nIssuerTrust goes back to the app in the response of 1.2 , the app shows it in the preview in section 7.2
Mini<--DW: 200 (response of 1.2) | issuanceSessionId , OfferUrl , ExpiresAt\nissuerTrust (Result , CheckedAt , RegistryReference)
@enduml
